{
  "dom_id": "step-q106420",
  "name": "Question 8",
  "problem": "Which of the following sets of parametric equations, defined for $t\\in (-\\infty ,\\infty ),$ generate the horizontal parabola given by the Cartesian equation ${y}^{2}=12x?$",
  "worked_solution": "The parametric equations of a horizontal parabola ${y}^{2}=4px$ that has its vertex at $(0,0)$ are\n\n$$\nx=p{t}^{2},\\,y=2pt,\n$$\n\nwhere $p$ is constant.\n\nComparing the given Cartesian equation with the general case ${y}^{2}=4px$ and solving for $p,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4px & =12x \\\\ 4p & =12 \\\\ p & =3.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the parametric equations of the parabola are\n\n$$\nx=(3){t}^{2},\\,y=2(3)t,\n$$\n\nwhich simplify to\n\n$$\nx=3{t}^{2},\\,y=6t.\n$$",
